WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:20.630
"That will be 25 cents, please," Henry said.

2
00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:23.352
He handed a cup of lemonade to Tiny.

3
00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:27.174
Tiny was Henry's neighbor and the tallest kid in the tenth grade.

4
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:30.916
Tiny was also one of the lemonade stand's best customers.

5
00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:36.236
He stopped by the stand to buy lemonade almost every day, sometimes more than once.

6
00:00:37.397 --> 00:00:38.117
"Here you go."

7
00:00:38.478 --> 00:00:40.099
Tiny handed over a few coins.

8
00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:42.181
"Thanks for the lemonade!"

9
00:00:42.201 --> 00:00:43.862
"You're welcome."

10
00:00:46.804 --> 00:00:49.006
After Tiny left, Henry looked at Cole.

11
00:00:49.026 --> 00:00:52.529
"I hope Maggie comes back soon," he said.

12
00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:54.831
"We're almost out of lemonade."

13
00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:57.774
Just then Nathan hurried over.

14
00:00:57.794 --> 00:01:00.436
"Hi, guys," said their friend.

15
00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:03.325
"How are the lemonade and detective businesses?"

16
00:01:03.345 --> 00:01:05.945
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said.

17
00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.246
"The lemonade business is great."

18
00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:10.627
"Yeah," Cole agreed.

19
00:01:10.647 --> 00:01:13.667
"But the detective business is a little slow."

20
00:01:13.688 --> 00:01:20.049
"It's a good thing we haven't been busy solving any mysteries this week, though," Henry reminded Cole.

21
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.310
"Otherwise we wouldn't have had enough time to work on our float."

22
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:26.571
Nathan looked interested.

23
00:01:26.591 --> 00:01:27.871
"A float?

24
00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:29.712
You mean for the parade?"

25
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:31.437
Henry nodded.

26
00:01:32.037 --> 00:01:35.660
Belltown's annual Summer Parade was coming up that Saturday afternoon.

27
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.822
Anyone in town could sign up to enter a float.

28
00:01:38.842 --> 00:01:41.864
"It's going to be awesome!"

29
00:01:42.064 --> 00:01:43.045
Cole told Nathan.

30
00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:46.987
"This is the first time The Lemonade Detectives are entering."

31
00:01:47.948 --> 00:01:48.709
Henry laughed.

32
00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:53.532
"It would have been hard for The Lemonade Detectives to enter a float last year.

33
00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:56.414
Our business didn't exist then!"

34
00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.195
"Good point."

35
00:01:58.475 --> 00:01:59.176
Cole grinned.

36
00:01:59.972 --> 00:02:03.354
"Anyway, we're sure to win the grand prize for Best Float."

37
00:02:03.374 --> 00:02:06.935
"That's what Maggie is hoping," Henry said.

38
00:02:06.955 --> 00:02:14.599
"She really wants that cash prize, especially since she spent all her money on that horse show last

39
00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:16.660
week." Cole pointed.

40
00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.241
"Speaking of Maggie, here she comes."

41
00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:21.702
Maggie was rushing toward them.

42
00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:25.804
She was clutching a pitcher of lemonade and a laptop computer.

43
00:02:26.764 --> 00:02:29.105
"You guys will never believe what I just found out!"

44
00:02:29.405 --> 00:02:30.165
she exclaimed.

45
00:02:30.185 --> 00:02:34.546
"There are going to be two prizes awarded at the parade this year!"

46
00:02:34.566 --> 00:02:36.607
"Two prizes?"

47
00:02:36.907 --> 00:02:37.587
Henry said.

48
00:02:37.607 --> 00:02:41.588
"Do you mean there's a first prize and a second prize?"

49
00:02:41.608 --> 00:02:46.590
"No, there will be two first prizes," Maggie said.

50
00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:49.430
"Huh?" Cole looked confused.

51
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.291
"How can there be two first prizes?"

52
00:02:53.392 --> 00:02:54.592
Maggie looked impatient.

53
00:02:55.368 --> 00:02:57.649
"I'm trying to tell you," she said.

54
00:02:57.669 --> 00:03:03.192
"The mayor will award a cash prize for the best float, just like he does every year.

55
00:03:04.113 --> 00:03:06.894
But there's also going to be a poll on the town website.

56
00:03:07.775 --> 00:03:10.737
Anyone in town can vote for his or her favorite float."

57
00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.818
"Wow, cool!"

58
00:03:13.098 --> 00:03:13.798
Nathan said.

59
00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:17.600
"Does the winner of the popular vote get a cash prize too?"

60
00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.902
"No," Maggie said.

61
00:03:19.922 --> 00:03:23.704
"But the popular vote winner gets to be interviewed on TV."

62
00:03:25.008 --> 00:03:26.608
"That could be fun," Cole said.

63
00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:29.429
"Not just fun," Maggie said.

64
00:03:29.449 --> 00:03:36.151
"It would be great publicity for both of my—I mean our—businesses."

65
00:03:37.031 --> 00:03:41.493
She waved a hand at the signs advertising the lemonade stand and the detective business.

66
00:03:44.273 --> 00:03:46.054
Henry grabbed the laptop and opened it.

67
00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.995
The screen showed Belltown's website.

68
00:03:50.715 --> 00:03:54.176
"It looks like the popular poll isn't open yet," he said.

69
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.540
"Of course it's not, silly."

70
00:03:56.761 --> 00:03:57.521
Maggie shrugged.

71
00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:00.421
"Nobody has seen any of the floats yet.

72
00:04:00.642 --> 00:04:01.962
They're all top secret."

73
00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.403
Henry scanned the website.

74
00:04:04.423 --> 00:04:09.984
"It says voting will start as soon as the parade is over on Saturday."

75
00:04:10.864 --> 00:04:12.465
Cole looked over Henry's shoulder.

76
00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.005
"What's that?"

77
00:04:14.265 --> 00:04:17.446
he asked, pointing to something at the bottom of the computer screen.

78
00:04:18.386 --> 00:04:20.127
Henry scrolled down for a better look.

79
00:04:20.147 --> 00:04:24.608
"It's a place where people can write comments about the parade.

80
00:04:25.308 --> 00:04:27.090
See? Here's a note from Mrs.

81
00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:32.655
Sweet." "It says, 'My float will be the sweetest treat in town,'" Maggie read.

82
00:04:32.675 --> 00:04:38.260
"Here's one from Miss Bishop, the lady who owns the jewelry store right across from the Sweet Shop."

83
00:04:39.181 --> 00:04:41.303
Cole leaned closer to read the comment.

84
00:04:42.263 --> 00:04:45.967
"She says, 'My float will win the gold medal for sure.'"

85
00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:47.748
Maggie snorted.

86
00:04:47.768 --> 00:04:51.392
"Those ladies can keep dreaming," she said.

87
00:04:52.236 --> 00:04:56.078
"The Lemonade Detectives are definitely going to win both of those prizes!"

88
00:04:56.098 --> 00:04:59.699
"I'll vote for you guys," Nathan promised.

89
00:05:00.459 --> 00:05:01.740
"What does your float look like?"

90
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.022
Henry opened his mouth to answer, but Maggie spoke first.

91
00:05:06.042 --> 00:05:09.443
"We can't tell you," she said to Nathan.

92
00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:11.064
"It's top secret."

93
00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.445
"Don't be silly, Maggie!"

94
00:05:13.705 --> 00:05:14.405
Cole laughed.

95
00:05:14.425 --> 00:05:16.846
"We can trust Nathan."

96
00:05:17.746 --> 00:05:18.907
Maggie looked uncertain.

97
00:05:18.927 --> 00:05:21.428
"Do you promise not to tell anyone?

98
00:05:22.408 --> 00:05:24.409
Especially your little sister, Nora.

99
00:05:24.589 --> 00:05:27.091
She has a big mouth."

100
00:05:27.111 --> 00:05:28.692
"I promise," Nathan said.

101
00:05:28.712 --> 00:05:35.075
"My sister is staying with my grandparents this week, so I couldn't tell her even if I wanted

102
00:05:35.135 --> 00:05:38.837
to." "Our float is really cool," Cole told him.

103
00:05:38.857 --> 00:05:44.841
"We made a huge lemon out of papier-mâché, and we're dressing it up to look like Sherlock Holmes."

104
00:05:44.861 --> 00:05:46.322
"Get it?"

105
00:05:46.542 --> 00:05:47.162
Henry said.

106
00:05:47.182 --> 00:05:50.084
"Sherlock Holmes is a famous detective.

107
00:05:51.032 --> 00:05:53.114
And we're The Lemonade Detectives."

108
00:05:54.094 --> 00:05:55.115
Nathan was laughing.

109
00:05:55.135 --> 00:05:57.697
"A lemon dressed like Sherlock Holmes?

110
00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.097
That's funny!"

111
00:06:00.899 --> 00:06:02.420
Suddenly Maggie spun around.

112
00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.702
"Hey!" she cried, pointing at a figure.

113
00:06:05.722 --> 00:06:07.323
"Who are you?

114
00:06:07.803 --> 00:06:08.964
Are you spying on us?"
